///
/// Holds no nonces between operations: each signing round generates fresh ones
/// and consumes them exactly once. That is not a style choice — reusing a FROST
/// nonce across two different messages **leaks the key share**, which is the
/// single most dangerous mistake available in this protocol and the reason the
/// API below hands the nonces straight to the coordinator rather than storing
/// them on `self`.
